    "text": "The San Antonio Spurs (57-18) travel to Chase Center to face the Golden State Warriors (36-39) on Wednesday night in NBA action. MORE: Ranking the top 15 NBA teams heading into April Advertisement Feb 11, 2026; San Francisco, California, USA; San Antonio Spurs forward Keldon Johnson (3) rebounds against the Golden State Warriors in the fourth quarter at Chase Center. Mandatory Credit: Eakin Howard-Imagn Images How to Watch San Antonio Spurs vs Golden State Warriors When: Wednesday, April 1, 2026 Time: 10:00 PM ET TV Channel: ESPN, ESPN Deportes Live Stream: Fubo (try for free) The Spurs continue to make their case as one of the favorites to be the Western Conference representative in the NBA Finals, posting a blistering 25-2 record over their last 27 games. They’ve won nine in a row, with each of the last five being by 15 points or more. Victor Wembanyama sits as one of the MVP favorites, with yet another ridiculous stat line in the Spurs’ most recent win over the Chicago Bulls, scoring 41 points with 16 rebounds, four assists, one steal, and three blocks. Golden State will make the NBA Playoffs, but is limping to the regular season finish line. Steph Curry is still out nursing an injured knee, while Al Horford, Quinten Post, and Will Richard are all day-to-day with their own injuries. Even with those struggles, the Warriors were able to put together a tidy three-game winning streak recently, albeit against three non-playoff teams (Dallas, Brooklyn, Washington). In their last game, the Warriors lost 116-93 on the road to the Denver Nuggets, as Brandon Podziemski and Kristaps Porzingis tied for the team lead with 23 points each. This is a great NBA matchup that you will not want to miss; make sure to tune in and catch all the action. Advertisement With Fubo, you can watch live television without cable on your phone, TV, or tablet. Fubo carries a wide array of sports and entertainment channels, including local sports packages and top national channels suc